  "body": "## What changed\n\n- All face meters and edge-curve meters of one shell pass share one pass budget (`Pass`, new `step_meter.rs`).\n- Each meter counts its first refusal in the pass one time. A refusal is a cap that ran out, a division that did not converge, or a boundary-search fault.\n- At `PASS_TRIPS` (3) trips the pass stops. Then each meter answers its fixed point, and each face in flight ends within one sweep.\n- The stopped pass is refused by name. The refusal names the first face or edge that really tripped. It adds: \"the tessellation stopped after 3 faces or edges ran out of evaluations; more of the model may be broken\".\n- A stopped pass is never \"continuous\". Thus no coarser mesh is kept for it.\n- A meter that the stop cut short is not a trip. Its `exhaust` and its search faults are not recorded. Thus a refusal never names a healthy face.\n- `Meter` moved from `step_guard.rs` to `step_meter.rs`. This keeps `step_guard.rs` under 400 lines (now 365).\n\n## Cause\n\nThe 150 M evaluation cap applied to each face, not to the pass. Each runaway face spent a full cap (10-15 s) before it tripped. A file with N runaway faces thus cost N caps divided by the core count.\n\n## Tests\n\nPins (red before the fix: yes):\n\n- `step_meter::tests::a_pass_with_many_runaway_faces_stops_after_a_few_trips`. A shell with 31 runaway faces. Before: `31 runaway faces spent 6200175 evaluations, bound 2200011`. After: under the bound (3 caps plus one cap for each worker thread).\n- `import_step_guard::a_shell_of_many_runaway_faces_is_refused_after_a_few_trips`. End to end: `bspline_discontinuous.step` with face #53 listed 40 more times. It is refused by name, and the refusal says that the pass stopped.\n- `step_meter::tests::the_pass_stops_at_the_trip_limit_and_a_stopped_meter_is_not_a_trip`\n- `step_meter::tests::a_stopped_pass_of_proven_faces_is_not_continuous`\n- `step_meter::tests::edge_trips_count_against_the_pass_budget`\n- `step_meter::tests::the_refusal_of_a_stopped_pass_says_it_stopped`\n- `step_meter::tests::a_pass_with_one_runaway_face_is_not_stopped` (unchanged behaviour below the limit)\n\nMutation checks. Each guard was removed, the pins were run, and the code was restored:\n\n- `spend` ignores a stopped pass: red.\n- `spend_many` ignores a stopped pass: red.\n- A stopped pass can be continuous: red.\n- `exhaust` on a stopped pass: red.\n- `flag` on a stopped pass: red.\n- Faces do not share the pass (the old code): red (4 pins).\n- Edges do not share the pass: red.\n- The refusal has no stop note: red.\n- The pass is not reset between passes: red.\n\nGate: `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` is green (lib plus 18 import suites, 78 s). These include `step_fidelity`, `large_models`, `model_fidelity`, `step_budget` and `import_step_guard_default_cap`. Healthy imports did not change. `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings` is clean.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The release heavy lanes (the measured corpus and the 150 M default-cap timing in release).\n- The kernel crate's test copy of the guard (`crates/kernel/tests/step_util/truck_guard.rs`). It is a separate test helper and this PR does not change it.\n\n## Overlaps\n\nNone in substance. Open PR #1738 lists these files only because of the drift of its stacked base. It does not change the STEP guard.\n\nDecisions: `docs/decisions/1599-pass-eval-budget.md`.\n\nEffort: high\n\nChangelog: STEP import stops a shell's tessellation pass after 3 faces or edges run out of evaluations, so a file with many broken faces is refused by name in bounded time (#1599)\n\nFixes #1599\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
